      "description": "Watch Chelsea vs Arsenal highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on January 14, 2026. On January 14, 2026 , the Carabao Cup served up a high-octane clash between Chelsea and Leeds United . This midweek fixture under the lights promised intensity as both sides looked to secure their progression in the tournament. Leeds Stuns the Bridge Leeds United started with a fearless attitude, taking the fight to their hosts from the opening whistle. Their persistence paid off in the 23rd minute when Tarik Muharemovic rose highest to meet a Harry Wilson cross following a corner, heading firmly into the net. Chelsea struggled to find their rhythm in the opening period, with Jamie Gittens seeing his efforts saved by Michael Zetterer . Frustration boiled over late in the half as Reggie Watson picked up a yellow card, leaving the Blues with plenty of work to do. The Palmer Effect The second half began with a shock as Brenden Aaronson doubled the visitors' lead in the 48th minute, finishing coolly after being set up by Lukas Nmecha . Facing an uphill battle, the introduction of Cole Palmer at halftime proved to be a tactical masterstroke. In the 53rd minute, Palmer converted a penalty after Pep Chavarría was fouled in the box. Just two minutes later, the playmaker struck again, firing a left-footed shot into the bottom corner to bring the scores level and ignite the home crowd. A Goal-Scoring Frenzy With the momentum firmly in their favor, Chelsea surged ahead. Pedro Neto made it 3-2 in the 60th minute with a clinical strike from distance, before Danny Welbeck added a fourth shortly after. Leeds United refused to surrender, and Dominic Calvert-Lewin pulled one back to make it 4-3 in the 75th minute, ensuring a tense finale. However, the quality of the Blues' substitutes continued to tell as they pushed for a decisive advantage. Sealing the Result As the clock ticked toward full-time, Valentín Barco found the bottom corner in the 80th minute to restore a two-goal cushion. Despite a late flurry of blocked attempts from a desperate Leeds side, the final word belonged to Danny Welbeck . In the fourth minute of stoppage time, Welbeck headed home his second of the night to seal a remarkable 6-3 victory. It was a breathless display of attacking football that saw Chelsea advance after a truly unforgettable second-half performance."
